# fleetclient/manifest — the files a colleague's computer gets from the hub
# (claude-fleet#1470, #1486): `curl -fsSL <hub>/install | sh`.
#
# One repo-relative path per line, in install order; `#` starts a comment. Each
# is served at GET /install/<path> (its SHA-256 in X-Ccquota-Sha256) and lands
# at <install home>/<path> (~/.claude/fleet) — the repo's own bin/ + conf/
# layout, so `$BIN/../conf/…` resolves there as in a checkout. An optional
# second word tags a line:
#   installer  the template GET /install serves with the hub's URL filled in;
#              never a download of its own
#   served     (issue #4826) served at /install/<path> like the rest, but NOT
#              installed: what only a hosting machine, a managed Mac or an admin
#              runs. The client fetches it on first use (fc_served,
#              bin/fleet-client-lib.sh) from where it came from, and the one-line
#              join / install commands curl it from the hub as before
# The format only grows (EPIC #4823 共同约定 3): an older installer that knows
# no `served` downloads such a line too — more files, never a broken client.
#
# This list is read in three places and maintained here only:
#   · fleetclient/embed.go       the hub — what to serve, which file is the installer
#   · bin/fleet-client-pack.sh   the copy into pack/ for the hub's build (every line)
#   · bin/fleet-install.sh       fetches it as GET /install/manifest and walks it
# and two tests hold it to the repo: TestFleetClientMatchesBin (Go) and
# bin/fleet-install-selftest.sh leg A (shell).
#
# What is installed (EPIC #4823 共同约定 1): a file stays only when a client
# action uses it — conf/client-runtime.list, made by bin/fleet-client-runtime.sh,
# whose --check holds the two lists together both ways — or the installer's own
# steps do. The client's scripts read bin/fleet-client-core.sh, never the
# machine's fleet-lib.sh (issue #4825); the Agent configuration package (hooks ·
# skills · commands · MCP · the mod) is 承载's, installed by `fleet host on`
# with the rest of the tree (issue #4826, the EPIC's decision 1).
bin/fleet-install.sh  installer
bin/fleet
bin/fleet-login.py
